# ─── secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository is public. Everything below is material that would be a real
# compromise if it were ever committed, listed first because a .gitignore is
# only useful for the mistake you have not made yet.
#
# scripts/setup-signing-key.sh writes its backup as handheld-repo-*.asc plus a
# passphrase file, and will happily do so into this directory if you point
# OUT_DIR here. scripts/publish-r2.sh exports the public key as
# keyring/handheld.gpg at publish time.
*.asc
*.gpg
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
handheld-repo-*
*passphrase*
*secret*
*credentials*
rclone.conf
.rclone.conf
.aws/
.config/rclone/
*.local.*
*.local
keyring/

# .env files, except the two this build genuinely uses. sources.env is tracked
# on purpose -- it is the pinned-refs manifest, not configuration, and it holds
# nothing secret. version.env is generated.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!sources.env
version.env

# ─── fetched patch content ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Resolved at build time from the refs in sources.env, never committed. The
# manifests in patches/series.d/ and patches/ogc.select are what make the stack
# reviewable; the .patch files belong to their upstreams.
#
# Flat only: patches/<product>/*.patch is committed on purpose -- that is where a
# patch with nothing to fetch it from lives.
patches/*.patch
patches/rocknix-staged/
dts/

# ─── generated by scripts/fetch-patches.sh ──────────────────────────────────
patches/series.generated
# per-product manifest of what was fetched into the shared flat patches/ dir;
# the union of these is what pruning protects
patches/.fetched.*
# flock target for the one-build-per-tree guard
.build.lock
.fetch-report.md
.staged-report.md
# tee'd by scripts/makepkg-and-report.sh so the job summary can quote the build
.makepkg.log
.rclone-err

# ─── build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
out/
src/
pkg/
*.pkg.tar.zst
*.pkg.tar.zst.sig
*.pkg.tar.xz
*.pkg.tar.xz.sig
.ccache/

# Kernel tarballs. .cache/ is where fetch-patches.sh puts the one it verified
# against kernel.org, and SRCDEST points makepkg at the same directory so it
# reuses that copy rather than downloading a second 150 MB one. The rooted globs
# catch anything that lands beside the PKGBUILD anyway.
.cache/
/linux-*.tar.xz
/linux-*.tar.gz

# ─── editor and OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
